## Purpose

This draft starts adding support for PEFT sequence-classification LoRA adapters whose trained classification head is stored through `modules_to_save`.

A sequence-classification adapter may contain both regular LoRA A/B weights for the backbone and a fully trained `score` or `classifier` module. vLLM currently rejects non-empty `modules_to_save` configurations and assumes that every adapter module consists of LoRA A/B tensors, preventing these adapters from being loaded correctly.

This draft introduces the loader-side representation needed for the feature:

- allow `score` and `classifier` in PEFT `modules_to_save`;
- introduce `LoRAFullModuleWeights` for full module weights and optional bias;
- separate full classification-head tensors from regular LoRA A/B tensors during checkpoint loading;
- store full modules separately in `LoRAModel.modules_to_save`;
- preserve full-module weights when cloning a `LoRAModel`;

This is intentionally a draft. The current PR does not yet apply the loaded classification head during inference.

Remaining work includes:

- [x] adding a LoRA-aware classification-head wrapper;
- [x] validating adapter head shapes against the runtime base head;
- [x] routing full classifier heads with request/prompt-level mappings  instead of token-level LoRA mappings;
- [x] handling adapter activation, slot reuse, LRU eviction, and reset;
- [x] adding mixed-adapter classification tests and Hugging Face PEFT parity evaluation;
- [x] documenting the supported scope and limitations.

FIX: #12829, #19623, #23719, #30058 and #57002.

